### 4. Context Propagation (internal/context/)

**Context Helpers:**
```go
NewRequestContext() (context.Context, context.CancelFunc)
WithRequestID(ctx, id) context.Context
RequestID(ctx) string
WithService(ctx, service) context.Context
Service(ctx) string
WithHostname(ctx, hostname) context.Context
Hostname(ctx) string
WithClientID(ctx, clientID) context.Context
ClientID(ctx) string
```

**Design Patterns:**
- Every public function accepts `ctx context.Context` as first parameter
- Every HTTP handler creates context from request
- Every outbound call passes context
- Every goroutine respects cancellation
- Values propagate through derived contexts
- Cancellation propagates to children
- Child cancellation does NOT affect parent

**Type Safety:**
- Uses unexported `contextKey` type to prevent collisions
- All key constants are unexported

