### Description

Implement bearer token authentication strategy that injects "Authorization: Bearer <secret>" header into requests. This is the most common API authentication method used by OpenAI, Anthropic, and most modern REST APIs.

Strategy registered as "bearer" in global registry.

### Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Create internal/auth/bearer.go with BearerStrategy struct
- [ ] Implement Apply(ctx context.Context, req *http.Request, secret string) error
- [ ] Set Authorization header: "Bearer {secret}"
- [ ] If Authorization header already exists, REPLACE it (don't append)
- [ ] Validate secret is not empty (return error if empty)
- [ ] Log header injection WITHOUT logging secret value
- [ ] Use CloneRequest() to avoid mutating original request
- [ ] Register strategy in init() using auth.Register("bearer", &BearerStrategy{})
- [ ] Write unit tests with mock http.Request
- [ ] Test: empty secret returns error
- [ ] Test: existing Authorization header is replaced
- [ ] Test: original request is not modified (verify via comparison)
- [ ] Test: header format is exactly "Bearer <secret>" (no extra spaces)
- [ ] Test coverage >= 85%

### Technical Notes

**Implementation Pattern:**
```go
// internal/auth/bearer.go (NEW)
package auth

import (
    "context"
    "fmt"
    "net/http"

    "github.com/bmf/chaperone/internal/errors"
    "github.com/bmf/chaperone/internal/log"
)

type BearerStrategy struct{}

func (s *BearerStrategy) Apply(ctx context.Context, req *http.Request, secret string) error {
    if secret == "" {
        return errors.ErrSecretNotFound
    }

    // Clone request to avoid mutation
    cloned := CloneRequest(req)

    // Set Authorization header
    cloned.Header.Set("Authorization", "Bearer "+secret)

    log.Debug(ctx, "injected bearer token authentication")

    *req = *cloned  // Copy back to original pointer
    return nil
}

func init() {
    Register("bearer", &BearerStrategy{})
}
```

**Security Considerations:**
- Secret NEVER logged (only log "injected bearer token authentication")
- Header set with Set() not Add() to prevent duplicate headers
- Empty secret rejected immediately

**Testing Pattern:**
```go
func TestBearerStrategy(t *testing.T) {
    req := httptest.NewRequest("GET", "https://api.example.com", nil)
    original := CloneRequest(req)

    strategy := &BearerStrategy{}
    err := strategy.Apply(context.Background(), req, "test-secret")

    require.NoError(t, err)
    assert.Equal(t, "Bearer test-secret", req.Header.Get("Authorization"))
    assert.Equal(t, original.URL.String(), req.URL.String())  // URL unchanged
}
```

