{"id":"CHAP-2oe","content_hash":"ffef0cdcde1f93b9c21408aa2a045c867cddf8707e1a62fda8faa6a895542cfd","title":"Verify AuthStrategy interface and add strategy registry","description":"Verify the AuthStrategy interface from Phase 0.1 meets implementation needs. Add strategy registry and request cloning helper.","design":"NOTE: The AuthStrategy interface is ALREADY DEFINED in Phase 0.1 (CHAP-dhf). This task adds the supporting infrastructure.\n\nIn internal/auth/:\n- Review strategy.go interface from Phase 0.1\n- Create strategy registry (map[string]AuthStrategy)\n- Add Register(name string, strategy AuthStrategy) function\n- Add Get(name string) (AuthStrategy, error) function\n- Add helper for request cloning: CloneRequest(req *http.Request) *http.Request\n  - Clone URL, headers, body if needed\n  - Preserve all request metadata\n  - Return new request that can be safely modified\n\nWrite tests:\n- Strategy registration tests\n- Strategy retrieval tests\n- Request cloning tests (ensure deep copy)","acceptance_criteria":"- Interface is well-defined and documented\n- Strategy registry works\n- Request cloning helper works correctly\n- Unit tests for registry","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:55:40.129137-07:00","updated_at":"2025-12-01T05:02:23.001193-07:00","closed_at":"2025-12-01T05:02:23.001193-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-2oe","depends_on_id":"CHAP-bwz","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:55:40.130732-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-2oe","depends_on_id":"CHAP-dhf","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:12:55.915023-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-30o","content_hash":"4b9956c630c7c5a605b22d79b300cdf3166af131e03e54b834a02611dbdfa26a","title":"Phase 0.5: Build test infrastructure (frameworks, helpers, fixtures)","description":"Set up comprehensive test infrastructure including test frameworks, certificate generation helpers, mock servers, test fixtures, and patterns. This MUST exist before writing feature code so tests can be written first.","design":"Install test dependencies:\n```bash\ngo get github.com/stretchr/testify\n```\n\nCreate test/helpers/certs.go:\n```go\n// GenerateTestCA creates CA for testing\nfunc GenerateTestCA(t *testing.T) (*x509.Certificate, *rsa.PrivateKey)\n\n// GenerateTestCert creates leaf certificate signed by test CA\nfunc GenerateTestCert(t *testing.T, ca *x509.Certificate, caKey *rsa.PrivateKey, hostname string) (*x509.Certificate, *rsa.PrivateKey)\n\n// TrustTestCA creates http.Client that trusts test CA\nfunc TrustTestCA(t *testing.T, caCert *x509.Certificate) *http.Client\n```\n\nCreate test/helpers/mock_server.go:\n```go\n// NewMockAPIServer creates test HTTP server\nfunc NewMockAPIServer(t *testing.T, handler http.Handler) *httptest.Server\n\n// NewMockTLSServer creates test HTTPS server\nfunc NewMockTLSServer(t *testing.T, handler http.Handler, cert *x509.Certificate, key *rsa.PrivateKey) *httptest.Server\n```\n\nCreate test/fixtures/configs/:\n- minimal.toml (bare minimum config)\n- openai.toml (example OpenAI config)\n- invalid.toml (for validation tests)\n\nCreate test/helpers/context.go:\n```go\n// NewTestContext creates context with request ID for testing\nfunc NewTestContext(t *testing.T) context.Context\n```\n\nCreate test patterns documentation in test/README.md:\n- Table-driven test pattern\n- Test naming conventions\n- Fixture usage\n- Test cleanup patterns\n- Integration test patterns\n\nConfigure coverage:\n- Add coverage reporting to Makefile\n- Set minimum coverage threshold (80%)\n\nWrite example tests demonstrating patterns:\n- test/helpers/example_test.go (shows how to use helpers)\n- test/integration/example_test.go (shows integration test pattern)","acceptance_criteria":"- testify installed and usable\n- Test CA generation works\n- Test certificate generation works\n- Mock HTTP server helpers work\n- Mock HTTPS server helpers work\n- Test fixtures exist and load correctly\n- Coverage reporting configured in Makefile\n- Example tests demonstrate patterns\n- Test README documents conventions\n- make test runs (even with just example tests)\n- make test-race runs without errors","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:09:48.223996-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-28T17:27:24.738917-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-28T17:27:24.738917-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-30o","depends_on_id":"CHAP-3q0","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:09:48.226538-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-3ot","content_hash":"71a0bc06346ba875cdcf7d25bd744be314ddc243da4bbc7b077251900bb6bab7","title":"Implement domain matching logic","description":"Implement logic to determine if a domain should be MITM'd based on service configuration. Exact match for MVP, defer wildcards.","design":"In internal/service/:\n- Create matcher.go with domain matching\n- Implement exact hostname matching\n- Create function: ShouldMITM(hostname string) bool\n- Look up hostname in service registry\n- Return true if service configured, false otherwise\n- Add logging for matching decisions\n- Defer wildcard/regex matching to post-MVP","acceptance_criteria":"- Exact hostname match works\n- Configured domains return true\n- Non-configured domains return false\n- Case-insensitive matching\n- Port stripping works (api.example.com:443 -\u003e api.example.com)\n- Unit tests for all match scenarios","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:52:43.162049-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-30T16:30:05.299393-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-30T16:30:05.299393-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-3ot","depends_on_id":"CHAP-na8","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:52:43.163779-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-3q0","content_hash":"58fe96283598a6b7851ad206fbb055ad1710896c0da9f9a12a6a1d14335bd67a","title":"Phase 0.4: Implement configuration framework (TOML parsing and validation)","description":"Build configuration system with TOML schema, parser, validator, and default values. Configuration must be available from day 1 so all components can be configurable rather than hard-coded.","design":"Create internal/config/config.go:\n\n**Configuration structure:**\n```go\ntype Config struct {\n    Server   ServerConfig\n    Services map[string]ServiceConfig\n    Logging  LoggingConfig\n}\n\ntype ServerConfig struct {\n    Address string `toml:\"address\"`\n    Port    int    `toml:\"port\"`\n    CAPath  string `toml:\"ca_path\"`\n}\n\ntype ServiceConfig struct {\n    HostPattern   string       `toml:\"host_pattern\"`\n    AuthStrategy  string       `toml:\"auth_strategy\"`\n    CredentialRef string       `toml:\"credential_ref\"`\n    Policy        PolicyConfig `toml:\"policy\"`\n}\n\ntype PolicyConfig struct {\n    AllowedMethods []string `toml:\"allowed_methods\"`\n    AllowedPaths   []string `toml:\"allowed_paths\"`\n    MaxBodyBytes   int64    `toml:\"max_body_bytes\"`\n}\n\ntype LoggingConfig struct {\n    Level  string `toml:\"level\"`\n    Format string `toml:\"format\"`\n}\n```\n\n**Configuration loading:**\n```go\nfunc Load(path string) (*Config, error) {\n    data, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n    if err != nil {\n        return nil, fmt.Errorf(\"read config: %w\", err)\n    }\n    \n    var cfg Config\n    if err := toml.Unmarshal(data, \u0026cfg); err != nil {\n        return nil, fmt.Errorf(\"parse config: %w\", err)\n    }\n    \n    if err := cfg.Validate(); err != nil {\n        return nil, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid config: %w\", err)\n    }\n    \n    cfg.SetDefaults()\n    return \u0026cfg, nil\n}\n```\n\n**Validation logic:**\n- Port in range 1-65535\n- Required fields present\n- Log level valid (debug, info, warn, error)\n- Auth strategy valid\n- Paths well-formed\n\n**Default values:**\n- Address: \"127.0.0.1\"\n- Port: 4010\n- CAPath: \"~/.config/chaperone/\"\n- LogLevel: \"info\"\n\nWrite tests for:\n- TOML parsing\n- Validation catches errors\n- Defaults applied correctly\n- Example configs load successfully","acceptance_criteria":"- Config loads from TOML file successfully\n- Validation catches invalid port numbers\n- Validation catches missing required fields\n- Validation catches invalid log levels\n- Default values applied when not specified\n- Example config (OpenAI) loads without errors\n- Test coverage \u003e= 85%\n- go test passes for all config scenarios","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:09:22.670796-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-28T17:27:18.95539-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-28T17:27:18.95539-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-3q0","depends_on_id":"CHAP-4an","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:09:22.672486-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-4an","content_hash":"f9b2f1455c325117481a25d982c9002cd713a82db5abebe9792e98d683148f63","title":"Phase 0.3: Build observability foundation (structured logging)","description":"Set up structured logging infrastructure with log/slog, request ID generation and propagation, context-aware logging, and log redaction for secrets. Logging MUST be in place before any feature code.","design":"Create internal/log/logger.go:\n\n**Global logger initialization:**\n```go\nvar logger *slog.Logger\n\nfunc init() {\n    handler := slog.NewJSONHandler(os.Stdout, \u0026slog.HandlerOptions{\n        Level: slog.LevelInfo,\n        ReplaceAttr: redactSensitiveFields,\n    })\n    logger = slog.New(handler)\n}\n```\n\n**Request ID management:**\n```go\n// WithRequestID creates context with unique request ID\nfunc WithRequestID(ctx context.Context) context.Context {\n    reqID := uuid.New().String()\n    return context.WithValue(ctx, requestIDKey, reqID)\n}\n\n// FromContext gets logger with request ID from context\nfunc FromContext(ctx context.Context) *slog.Logger {\n    reqID := RequestIDFromContext(ctx)\n    return logger.With(\"request_id\", reqID)\n}\n```\n\n**Standard logging methods:**\n```go\nfunc Info(ctx context.Context, msg string, args ...any)\nfunc Error(ctx context.Context, msg string, err error, args ...any)\nfunc Debug(ctx context.Context, msg string, args ...any)\nfunc Warn(ctx context.Context, msg string, args ...any)\n```\n\n**Duration logging:**\n```go\nfunc LogDuration(ctx context.Context, operation string, start time.Time)\n```\n\n**Field redaction:**\n- Redact Authorization headers\n- Redact any field containing \"secret\", \"password\", \"token\", \"key\"\n- Replace with \"[REDACTED]\"\n\nWrite tests for:\n- Request ID propagation\n- Log level filtering\n- Field redaction\n- JSON output format","acceptance_criteria":"- Logger outputs valid JSON to stdout\n- Request IDs are unique per request\n- Request ID propagates through context correctly\n- Authorization headers are redacted in logs\n- Secret values never appear in logs\n- Log levels work correctly (debug, info, warn, error)\n- Duration logging works and reports milliseconds\n- Test coverage \u003e= 85%\n- go test -race passes","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:09:03.232671-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-28T17:27:13.303491-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-28T17:27:13.303491-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-4an","depends_on_id":"CHAP-7no","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:09:03.234345-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-4iy","content_hash":"1e428d5f05c20a60012b10c06d7d696822c0b436460ead04653adc00a985ff62","title":"Write integration test for transparent HTTPS tunneling","description":"Create integration test that validates transparent HTTPS tunneling works correctly for arbitrary domains (e.g., google.com).","design":"In test/integration/:\n- Create tunnel_test.go\n- Start chaperone server in test\n- Configure HTTP client to use proxy\n- Make HTTPS request to google.com\n- Verify response is correct\n- Verify tunnel is transparent (no MITM yet)\n- Test connection cleanup\n- Test error handling (invalid host, timeout)","acceptance_criteria":"- Test starts and stops proxy server\n- HTTPS request through proxy succeeds\n- Response matches direct request\n- No certificate warnings (pure tunnel)\n- Test cleans up resources\n- Test runs in CI environment","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:50:49.702996-07:00","updated_at":"2025-12-01T01:44:19.040745-07:00","closed_at":"2025-12-01T01:44:19.040745-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-4iy","depends_on_id":"CHAP-ecl","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:50:49.704633-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-4iy","depends_on_id":"CHAP-b2i","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:51:36.481515-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-4tx","content_hash":"d89a084c3391171aaf195b83529739fe236ef45c89740535c723a28beda5c2d4","title":"Integrate service engine with MITM handler","description":"Wire service engine, secret providers, and auth strategies into MITM request handler.","design":"In internal/proxy/:\n- Modify MITM handler to lookup service by hostname\n- Fetch secret using service's credential_ref\n- Apply auth strategy using fetched secret\n- Enforce policies before forwarding request\n- Return 403 if policy denies request\n- Return 503 if secret fetch fails\n- Return 502 if upstream connection fails\n- Log all decisions and errors\n- Handle edge cases gracefully","acceptance_criteria":"- Service lookup works in request handler\n- Secret fetching integrated\n- Auth strategy application integrated\n- Policy enforcement integrated\n- Correct error responses for each failure mode\n- Integration test validates full flow\n- Logs show complete request lifecycle","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:56:21.992935-07:00","updated_at":"2025-12-01T05:02:40.14582-07:00","closed_at":"2025-12-01T05:02:40.14582-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-4tx","depends_on_id":"CHAP-pzr","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:56:21.994893-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-4tx","depends_on_id":"CHAP-a1z","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:57:33.678887-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-4tx","depends_on_id":"CHAP-i81","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:57:39.358085-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-4tx","depends_on_id":"CHAP-71t","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:57:45.013957-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-4tx","depends_on_id":"CHAP-c2s","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:57:50.670597-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-5e3","content_hash":"349f3205bea0cfd77ffdc7aecd124cf750e1a5d1c157965d8e082a675b1621c6","title":"Phase 0.6: Implement context propagation patterns","description":"Define context.Context usage patterns, create context value helpers, document timeout strategies, and establish cancellation patterns. Context must be used consistently from day 1.","design":"Create internal/context/context.go:\n\n**Context keys:**\n```go\ntype contextKey string\n\nconst (\n    requestIDKey  contextKey = \"request_id\"\n    serviceKey    contextKey = \"service\"\n    hostnameKey   contextKey = \"hostname\"\n)\n```\n\n**Context creation:**\n```go\n// NewRequestContext creates context with standard timeout\nfunc NewRequestContext() (context.Context, context.CancelFunc) {\n    return context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 60*time.Second)\n}\n```\n\n**Context value helpers:**\n```go\nfunc WithRequestID(ctx context.Context, id string) context.Context\nfunc RequestID(ctx context.Context) string\n\nfunc WithService(ctx context.Context, service string) context.Context\nfunc Service(ctx context.Context) string\n\nfunc WithHostname(ctx context.Context, hostname string) context.Context\nfunc Hostname(ctx context.Context) string\n```\n\nDocument patterns in internal/context/README.md:\n- Every public function accepts ctx as first parameter\n- Every HTTP handler creates context from request: ctx := r.Context()\n- Every outbound call passes context\n- Every goroutine respects context cancellation\n- Timeout patterns (use context.WithTimeout)\n- Cancellation patterns (defer cancel())\n\nWrite tests for:\n- Value storage and retrieval\n- Context propagation through call stack\n- Timeout behavior\n- Cancellation behavior","acceptance_criteria":"- Context helpers compile and work\n- Request ID helper stores and retrieves correctly\n- Service helper stores and retrieves correctly\n- Hostname helper stores and retrieves correctly\n- NewRequestContext creates context with 60s timeout\n- Context cancellation works correctly\n- Pattern documentation is clear\n- Test coverage \u003e= 85%\n- go test -race passes","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:10:06.181624-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-28T17:27:30.625556-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-28T17:27:30.625556-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-5e3","depends_on_id":"CHAP-30o","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:10:06.183361-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-5t0","content_hash":"1b43b4979a7959f8f9558c3561bd682027a9d74306df9583b33f24e416560e3a","title":"Phase 0.8: Build graceful shutdown infrastructure","description":"Implement shutdown manager for coordinating graceful shutdown of all components. This must be in place before components are built so they can register shutdown handlers from the start.","design":"Create internal/shutdown/shutdown.go:\n\n**Shutdown Manager:**\n```go\ntype Manager struct {\n    shutdownFuncs []func(ctx context.Context) error\n    shutdownOnce  sync.Once\n    logger        *slog.Logger\n}\n\nfunc NewManager(logger *slog.Logger) *Manager\n\n// Register adds shutdown function (called in LIFO order)\nfunc (m *Manager) Register(fn func(ctx context.Context) error)\n\n// WaitForShutdown blocks until SIGTERM/SIGINT received\nfunc (m *Manager) WaitForShutdown() error\n\n// Shutdown executes all registered functions with timeout\nfunc (m *Manager) Shutdown(timeout time.Duration) error\n```\n\n**Signal handling:**\n- Listen for SIGTERM and SIGINT\n- Execute shutdown functions in reverse order (LIFO)\n- Each function gets context with timeout\n- Collect all errors with errors.Join\n- Log shutdown progress\n\n**Usage pattern:**\n```go\nfunc (s *Server) Run(shutdownMgr *shutdown.Manager) error {\n    // Register shutdown handler\n    shutdownMgr.Register(func(ctx context.Context) error {\n        log.Info(\"shutting down HTTP server\")\n        return s.httpServer.Shutdown(ctx)\n    })\n    \n    // Start server\n    go s.httpServer.ListenAndServe()\n    \n    // Wait for shutdown signal\n    return shutdownMgr.WaitForShutdown()\n}\n```\n\nWrite tests for:\n- Function registration\n- LIFO execution order\n- Timeout handling\n- Error collection\n- Signal handling (using os.Signal channel)","acceptance_criteria":"- Shutdown manager compiles and works\n- Functions registered are called in LIFO order\n- Timeout is enforced (context cancellation)\n- Errors from multiple functions are collected\n- SIGTERM triggers shutdown\n- SIGINT triggers shutdown\n- Shutdown only runs once (sync.Once)\n- Test coverage \u003e= 85%\n- go test -race passes","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:10:26.728019-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-28T17:27:36.37102-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-28T17:27:36.37102-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-5t0","depends_on_id":"CHAP-5e3","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:10:26.730386-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-5v5","content_hash":"a01503536fcc769f6e5bfd3252b5c15a21dea550830af92b14a7e4afcbda4316","title":"Implement CA certificate generation and storage","description":"Generate local CA certificate and private key on first run, store securely in ~/.config/chaperone/ with appropriate permissions.","design":"In internal/mitm/:\n- Create ca.go with CA generation logic\n- Generate RSA 4096-bit private key\n- Create self-signed CA certificate (10 year validity)\n- Store CA key at ~/.config/chaperone/ca-key.pem (0600 permissions)\n- Store CA cert at ~/.config/chaperone/ca-cert.pem (0644 permissions)\n- Check if CA exists on startup, generate if missing\n- Add CA loading function for cert signing\n- Log CA generation and loading events","acceptance_criteria":"- CA key generated with correct key size\n- CA certificate is valid self-signed cert\n- Files stored in correct location\n- Permissions are correct (0600 for key, 0644 for cert)\n- CA loads successfully on subsequent runs\n- Unit tests for CA generation\n- CA can be used to sign certificates","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:52:31.830406-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-30T17:04:05.557136-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-30T17:04:05.557136-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-5v5","depends_on_id":"CHAP-na8","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:52:31.831761-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-6l4","content_hash":"1532cbf381a14a6b05419f12c73cf96ec9191f2b56be6788fca1221c885ed45c","title":"Add structured logging with log/slog","description":"Set up structured logging infrastructure using Go's stdlib log/slog for consistent, parseable logs throughout the application.","design":"In internal/audit/:\n- Create logger.go with logger initialization\n- Configure slog with JSON handler\n- Define log level configuration (debug, info, warn, error)\n- Create request context logger with request_id\n- Add helper methods for common log patterns\n- Configure log output (stdout for MVP)\n- Add timestamp and structured fields","acceptance_criteria":"- Logger outputs JSON format\n- Logs include timestamp and level\n- Request ID propagates through context\n- Different log levels work correctly\n- No log output in test mode (configurable)\n- Unit tests for logger configuration","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:50:44.040707-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-26T03:11:28.855779-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-26T03:11:28.855779-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-6l4","depends_on_id":"CHAP-ecl","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:50:44.042338-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-71t","content_hash":"8649bc8049fdfb6ddc3d9696abb860d9fe4c4065dd8cc4c47f719bf0888fdcde","title":"Implement bearer token auth strategy","description":"Implement bearer token authentication strategy that injects Authorization: Bearer header.","design":"In internal/auth/:\n- Create bearer.go with BearerStrategy struct\n- Implement Apply() method\n- Set Authorization header: \"Bearer {secret}\"\n- Handle existing Authorization header (replace it)\n- Log header injection (without logging secret value)\n- Register strategy as \"bearer\"\n- Write unit tests with mock requests","acceptance_criteria":"- Authorization header set correctly\n- Bearer prefix added\n- Existing Authorization header replaced\n- Secret not logged\n- Unit tests verify header injection\n- Request is properly cloned","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:55:45.771373-07:00","updated_at":"2025-12-01T05:02:28.769793-07:00","closed_at":"2025-12-01T05:02:28.769793-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-71t","depends_on_id":"CHAP-bwz","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:55:45.773515-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-71t","depends_on_id":"CHAP-2oe","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:56:56.756755-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-7no","content_hash":"415227160487e77db9a45f265c4577649191b98af99a0e318bf01740a5661188","title":"Phase 0.2: Create error handling framework","description":"Build unified error handling system with sentinel errors, structured error types, HTTP status mapping, and safe client message generation. This ensures consistent error handling across all components.","design":"Create internal/errors/errors.go:\n\n**Sentinel errors (use errors.Is):**\n```go\nvar (\n    ErrSecretNotFound    = errors.New(\"secret not found\")\n    ErrPermissionDenied  = errors.New(\"permission denied\")\n    ErrTimeout           = errors.New(\"operation timeout\")\n    ErrPolicyViolation   = errors.New(\"policy violation\")\n    ErrInvalidConfig     = errors.New(\"invalid configuration\")\n    ErrUpstreamError     = errors.New(\"upstream error\")\n)\n```\n\n**Structured error types (use errors.As):**\n```go\ntype SecretError struct {\n    Provider string\n    Ref      string\n    Cause    error\n}\n\ntype PolicyError struct {\n    PolicyType string // \"path\", \"method\", \"body_size\"\n    Value      string\n    Cause      error\n}\n\ntype ConfigError struct {\n    Field   string\n    Value   string\n    Cause   error\n}\n```\n\n**HTTP status mapping:**\n```go\nfunc HTTPStatus(err error) int {\n    // Maps internal errors to appropriate HTTP status codes\n}\n```\n\n**Safe client messages:**\n```go\nfunc ClientMessage(err error) string {\n    // Returns sanitized error messages safe to send to clients\n    // Redacts internal details for security\n}\n```\n\nWrite comprehensive tests for all error types, wrapping behavior, and HTTP mapping.","acceptance_criteria":"- All sentinel errors defined\n- All structured error types implement error interface\n- Unwrap() methods work correctly for error chains\n- HTTPStatus() returns correct status for all error types\n- ClientMessage() redacts sensitive information\n- Test coverage \u003e= 90% for error package\n- go test -race passes (no races in error handling)","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:08:44.411581-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-28T17:27:07.539561-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-28T17:27:07.539561-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-7no","depends_on_id":"CHAP-dhf","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:08:44.413591-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-8ft","content_hash":"d315568fbdad5e042bae56b925683e331398c4eb03b8b989c960c8f75200133a","title":"Phase 3: Secret Management - Provider System","description":"Design and implement pluggable secret provider system with env: and file: providers for MVP, including credential_ref parsing and secret caching.","design":"- Define SecretProvider interface\n- Implement credential_ref parser (protocol:path)\n- Implement provider registry\n- Implement env: provider (os.Getenv)\n- Implement file: provider with permission checks (0600)\n- Implement secret caching with TTL (5 minutes)\n- Define error types for secret operations","acceptance_criteria":"- SecretProvider interface defined and documented\n- env:VAR_NAME retrieves from environment\n- file:/path/to/secret reads file content\n- file: provider enforces 0600 permissions\n- Secret cache works with TTL\n- Unit tests for all providers pass\n- Integration test fetches secrets successfully","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:49:04.92313-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-26T02:49:04.92313-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-8ft","depends_on_id":"CHAP-na8","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:54:11.228701-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-8tw","content_hash":"15ae9f61f9898a3846ce662a3e0a89dce20a9e5efade8c305d0711aa21ef678e","title":"Implement CLI commands (init, run) using cobra","description":"Implement CLI framework with cobra, add 'chaperone init' and 'chaperone run' commands. CLI must load config from Phase 0.4 and use logging from Phase 0.3.","design":"Install cobra:\n```bash\ngo get github.com/spf13/cobra\n```\n\nCreate cmd/chaperone/main.go:\n```go\nfunc main() {\n    if err := cmd.Execute(); err != nil {\n        os.Exit(1)\n    }\n}\n```\n\nCreate cmd/chaperone/cmd/root.go:\n```go\nvar rootCmd = \u0026cobra.Command{\n    Use:   \"chaperone\",\n    Short: \"Local credential-injecting HTTPS proxy\",\n}\n\nfunc Execute() error {\n    return rootCmd.Execute()\n}\n\nfunc init() {\n    rootCmd.AddCommand(initCmd)\n    rootCmd.AddCommand(runCmd)\n}\n```\n\nCreate cmd/chaperone/cmd/init.go:\n```go\nvar initCmd = \u0026cobra.Command{\n    Use:   \"init [service]\",\n    Short: \"Initialize configuration for a service\",\n    Args:  cobra.ExactArgs(1),\n    RunE:  runInit,\n}\n\nfunc runInit(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {\n    // Load template for service (openai, anthropic, etc.)\n    // Write config to ~/.config/chaperone/config.toml\n    // Log success\n}\n```\n\nCreate cmd/chaperone/cmd/run.go:\n```go\nvar runCmd = \u0026cobra.Command{\n    Use:   \"run\",\n    Short: \"Start the proxy server\",\n    RunE:  runServer,\n}\n\nfunc runServer(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {\n    // Load config using Phase 0.4 config.Load()\n    // Initialize logger using Phase 0.3 log package\n    // Create shutdown manager using Phase 0.8\n    // Start server (Phase 1+ implementation)\n    // Wait for shutdown signal\n}\n```\n\nCreate templates in cmd/chaperone/templates/:\n- openai.toml.tmpl\n- anthropic.toml.tmpl\n\nWrite tests for:\n- Command parsing\n- Template loading\n- Config file creation","acceptance_criteria":"- chaperone --version works\n- chaperone --help shows usage\n- chaperone init openai creates config file\n- chaperone run loads config successfully\n- chaperone run starts server (when server implemented)\n- Templates exist for openai and anthropic\n- Test coverage \u003e= 80%","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:13:53.445833-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-28T17:26:30.548732-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-28T17:26:30.548732-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-8tw","depends_on_id":"CHAP-5t0","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:13:53.447748-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-90r","content_hash":"78825a0dc9e05dd987875d17927c3cbde11ef69161c38df77bfb2ef3b088713d","title":"Implement HTTP request proxying through MITM","description":"Forward decrypted HTTP request from client to upstream server and proxy response back through client TLS connection.","design":"In internal/proxy/:\n- Parse HTTP request from client TLS connection\n- Forward request to upstream via outbound client\n- Stream response back to client TLS connection\n- Preserve all HTTP headers and status codes\n- Handle chunked encoding correctly\n- Implement backpressure (io.Copy)\n- Handle request/response errors\n- Log request/response metadata\n- Handle connection cleanup on both sides","acceptance_criteria":"- HTTP request forwarded correctly\n- Response streamed back without buffering\n- Headers preserved accurately\n- Status codes forwarded correctly\n- Chunked encoding works\n- Large responses (10MB+) work\n- Connection cleanup is proper\n- No memory leaks with streaming\n- Integration test with real API","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:53:05.46248-07:00","updated_at":"2025-12-01T00:00:56.030921-07:00","closed_at":"2025-12-01T00:00:56.030921-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-90r","depends_on_id":"CHAP-na8","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:53:05.463954-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-90r","depends_on_id":"CHAP-e4n","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:53:44.884681-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-90r","depends_on_id":"CHAP-btx","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:53:59.924829-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-a1z","content_hash":"b15f246b89cce4d5eefe302d612d86d7b16eae0144317a14f674b021d21a21a8","title":"Implement service registry and lookup","description":"Implement service registry that stores and looks up services by hostname.","design":"In internal/service/:\n- Create registry.go with Registry struct\n- Use map[string]*Service keyed by host_pattern\n- Implement Register(service *Service) error\n- Implement Lookup(hostname string) (*Service, bool)\n- Exact match for MVP (defer wildcards)\n- Handle case-insensitive matching\n- Strip port from hostname (api.example.com:443 -\u003e api.example.com)\n- Thread-safe read access (read-only after load for MVP)\n- Add ListAll() for debugging","acceptance_criteria":"- Services register successfully\n- Lookup returns correct service\n- Case-insensitive matching works\n- Port stripping works\n- Missing services return false\n- Thread-safe for concurrent reads\n- Unit tests for all scenarios","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:56:02.785788-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-30T16:29:56.474711-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-30T16:29:56.474711-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-a1z","depends_on_id":"CHAP-pzr","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:56:02.787434-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-a1z","depends_on_id":"CHAP-qkq","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:57:08.045355-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-b2i","content_hash":"592c9e20315fc1a129091b1c9ab6369323167d54668aee51680c4a93d16ed91c","title":"Implement CONNECT tunnel handler with bidirectional streaming","description":"Implement CONNECT method handler that establishes bidirectional tunnels for HTTPS traffic. This is critical for transparent proxying.","design":"In internal/proxy/:\n- Create tunnel.go with CONNECT handler\n- Parse CONNECT request (extract host:port)\n- Hijack the client connection (Hijacker interface)\n- Establish TCP connection to upstream host\n- Send 200 Connection Established to client\n- Implement bidirectional io.Copy with goroutines\n- Handle connection cleanup and error propagation\n- Add context cancellation for cleanup\n- Log tunnel establishment and closure\n- Handle timeout for upstream connection","acceptance_criteria":"- CONNECT requests accepted\n- Upstream connection established\n- Bidirectional tunnel works (both directions)\n- Connection cleanup happens properly\n- No goroutine leaks (verified with pprof)\n- Unit test with mock connections\n- Integration test with real HTTPS site","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:50:38.390964-07:00","updated_at":"2025-12-01T01:44:13.006072-07:00","closed_at":"2025-12-01T01:44:13.006072-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-b2i","depends_on_id":"CHAP-ecl","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:50:38.392705-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-b2i","depends_on_id":"CHAP-jds","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:51:30.831455-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-btx","content_hash":"6f830096d246340496391c38e86626e9e144875db623bfc4419d3474decc5f6a","title":"Implement TLS connection to upstream server","description":"Establish standard TLS connection to upstream API server with proper certificate validation using system trust store.","design":"In internal/client/:\n- Create client.go with outbound HTTPS client\n- Create tls.Config with system cert pool\n- Set appropriate timeouts (30s connect, 60s read/write)\n- Create http.Client with custom Transport\n- Configure connection pooling (MaxIdleConnsPerHost: 100)\n- Enable HTTP/2 support\n- Respect corporate proxy settings (HTTP_PROXY env var)\n- NEVER set InsecureSkipVerify\n- Log connection establishment","acceptance_criteria":"- TLS connection to upstream succeeds\n- Certificate validation uses system trust\n- Expired/invalid certs rejected\n- Connection pooling works\n- Timeouts enforced\n- HTTP_PROXY environment variable respected\n- Unit test with mock server\n- Integration test with real API","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:52:59.810826-07:00","updated_at":"2025-12-01T00:00:50.208639-07:00","closed_at":"2025-12-01T00:00:50.208639-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-btx","depends_on_id":"CHAP-na8","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:52:59.812965-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-bwz","content_hash":"a8635f3d0af22f49c0cfea6ddf76c8de1d9b45b3a3a173c9a7f4376c9d5419fb","title":"Phase 4: Authentication - Strategy System","description":"Design and implement pluggable authentication strategy system with bearer token and header template strategies for MVP.","design":"- Define AuthStrategy interface\n- Implement strategy registry\n- Implement bearer token strategy (Authorization header)\n- Implement header template strategy (custom headers)\n- Request cloning mechanism to avoid mutations\n- Strategy selection based on service config","acceptance_criteria":"- AuthStrategy interface defined and documented\n- Bearer strategy injects Authorization header correctly\n- Header strategy injects custom headers\n- Original request is not modified\n- Unit tests for all strategies pass\n- Integration test verifies header injection","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:49:10.585261-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-26T02:49:10.585261-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-bwz","depends_on_id":"CHAP-8ft","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:57:56.311802-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-c2s","content_hash":"1010a991054d628f49eaf3f75f55dbf14c1b8c17353d9afe34cf65ca4a4e4835","title":"Implement path and method policy enforcement","description":"Implement policy enforcement for allowed paths and methods, returning 403 for violations.","design":"In internal/service/:\n- Create policy.go with enforcement functions\n- Implement CheckPath(path string, allowedPaths []string) bool\n- Use glob matching for paths (e.g., /v1/* matches /v1/chat)\n- Implement CheckMethod(method string, allowedMethods []string) bool\n- Use exact string match for methods\n- Implement CheckBodySize(contentLength int64, maxBytes int64) bool\n- Create enforcement function that checks all policies\n- Return appropriate HTTP 403 responses for violations\n- Log policy violations","acceptance_criteria":"- Path glob matching works (/v1/* matches /v1/chat)\n- Disallowed paths return false\n- Method checking works\n- Body size checking works\n- Policy violations logged\n- Unit tests for all policy types\n- Edge cases handled (empty allowlists, etc.)","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:56:08.45607-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-30T16:30:14.024489-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-30T16:30:14.024489-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-c2s","depends_on_id":"CHAP-pzr","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:56:08.458406-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-c2s","depends_on_id":"CHAP-qkq","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:57:13.677891-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-dhf","content_hash":"3400c6a542d1b715e6d3bc4b1fb42eb19eddfaa1fde0f9a5961d77360cae6a14","title":"Phase 0.1: Define all core interfaces before implementations","description":"Define ALL major interfaces with full godoc BEFORE any implementations. This is interface-first design - contracts are defined and agreed upon before concrete code is written.","design":"Create interface definitions in appropriate packages:\n\n**internal/secrets/provider.go:**\n```go\n// SecretProvider retrieves secrets from a backend storage system.\n// Implementations must be safe for concurrent use.\ntype SecretProvider interface {\n    // Fetch retrieves a secret by reference.\n    // Returns ErrSecretNotFound if secret doesn't exist.\n    // Returns ErrPermissionDenied if access is denied.\n    // Returns ErrTimeout if operation times out.\n    Fetch(ctx context.Context, ref string) (string, error)\n}\n```\n\n**internal/auth/strategy.go:**\n```go\n// AuthStrategy applies authentication to an HTTP request.\n// Implementations must NOT modify the original request.\ntype AuthStrategy interface {\n    // Apply injects authentication into the request.\n    // The request may be cloned if modification is needed.\n    Apply(ctx context.Context, req *http.Request, secret string) error\n}\n```\n\n**internal/service/registry.go:**\n```go\n// ServiceRegistry stores and retrieves service configurations.\ntype ServiceRegistry interface {\n    // Register adds a service to the registry.\n    Register(service *Service) error\n    \n    // Lookup finds a service by hostname.\n    Lookup(hostname string) (*Service, bool)\n    \n    // ListAll returns all registered services.\n    ListAll() []*Service\n}\n```\n\n**internal/service/policy.go:**\n```go\n// PolicyEnforcer checks requests against service policies.\ntype PolicyEnforcer interface {\n    // CheckPath verifies request path is allowed.\n    CheckPath(path string, policy *Policy) error\n    \n    // CheckMethod verifies HTTP method is allowed.\n    CheckMethod(method string, policy *Policy) error\n    \n    // CheckBodySize verifies request size is within limits.\n    CheckBodySize(size int64, policy *Policy) error\n}\n```\n\n**internal/audit/logger.go:**\n```go\n// AuditLogger records proxy activity.\ntype AuditLogger interface {\n    // LogRequest records a proxied request.\n    LogRequest(ctx context.Context, entry *RequestLog) error\n}\n```\n\nAlso define core structs:\n- Service (host_pattern, auth_strategy, credential_ref, policy)\n- Policy (allowed_methods, allowed_paths, max_body_bytes)\n- RequestLog (timestamp, request_id, service, method, path, status, etc.)","acceptance_criteria":"- All interfaces defined with complete godoc\n- Interface methods clearly document parameters and return values\n- Error types are specified in godoc\n- Concurrency safety requirements documented\n- All core structs defined\n- No implementations yet (interfaces only)\n- Interfaces reviewed for extensibility\n- go build succeeds (interfaces compile)","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:08:12.081636-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-28T17:27:01.311059-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-28T17:27:01.311059-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-dhf","depends_on_id":"CHAP-pmn","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:08:12.083277-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-e4n","content_hash":"e12b329775cbf5c4769452070d1381340e1a33dadb72568b66f9e4c36c39b8a0","title":"Implement TLS handshake with client (MITM mode)","description":"After receiving CONNECT request for managed domain, establish TLS connection with client using generated certificate.","design":"In internal/proxy/:\n- Modify tunnel handler to check if domain should be MITM'd\n- If MITM: Generate/retrieve certificate for domain\n- Create tls.Config with generated certificate\n- Wrap hijacked connection with tls.Server\n- Complete TLS handshake with client\n- Read HTTP request from TLS connection\n- Handle handshake errors gracefully\n- Log TLS handshake success/failure","acceptance_criteria":"- TLS handshake completes successfully\n- Client accepts generated certificate (when CA trusted)\n- HTTP request successfully read from TLS\n- Handshake errors logged appropriately\n- Non-MITM domains still use transparent tunnel\n- Unit test with mock TLS connection\n- Integration test with real client","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:52:54.131083-07:00","updated_at":"2025-12-01T00:00:44.272518-07:00","closed_at":"2025-12-01T00:00:44.272518-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-e4n","depends_on_id":"CHAP-na8","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:52:54.133225-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-e4n","depends_on_id":"CHAP-w9q","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:53:33.56196-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-e4n","depends_on_id":"CHAP-3ot","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:53:39.230133-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-ecl","content_hash":"56c0c6804bdc740ff5c94d9dbae4949e0c772be03d53844e30d3c5f278f4d4ef","title":"Phase 1: Foundation - Project Infrastructure and Basic Proxy","description":"Establish project foundation with Go module, directory structure, basic HTTP proxy server, and CONNECT tunnel support. This phase creates the foundational patterns and infrastructure for the entire project.","design":"- Initialize Go module with github.com/bmf/chaperone path\n- Create standard Go project structure (cmd/, internal/, etc.)\n- Implement basic HTTP proxy server using stdlib net/http\n- Implement CONNECT tunnel handler with connection hijacking\n- Add structured logging with log/slog\n- Add CLI framework (cobra or stdlib)\n- Validate transparent tunneling works for arbitrary HTTPS domains","acceptance_criteria":"- go.mod file exists and is valid\n- Project directory structure is complete\n- Basic proxy accepts CONNECT requests\n- Bidirectional tunnel works (io.Copy)\n- Integration test passes for HTTPS tunnel to google.com\n- chaperone run command starts server\n- Structured logs output to stdout","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:48:53.58546-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-28T17:30:26.566075-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-28T17:30:26.566075-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-ecl","depends_on_id":"CHAP-hbj","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:10:41.19371-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-hbj","content_hash":"7853b55405440564d053d18c53dabf55a81a82111d9ed8841534d5a41cb2c6d6","title":"Phase 0: Foundation Infrastructure - Build Before Features","description":"Establish rock-solid foundation BEFORE any feature implementation. This phase defines all interfaces, error handling patterns, observability infrastructure, configuration framework, test infrastructure, context propagation, and graceful shutdown. NO feature code is written until Phase 0 is complete.","design":"Phase 0 is the CRITICAL FOUNDATION that enables test-driven, interface-first, observable development for all subsequent phases.\n\nComponents:\n- 0.1: Core Interfaces - Define ALL interfaces before implementations\n- 0.2: Error Handling Framework - Sentinel errors, error types, HTTP mapping, safe client messages\n- 0.3: Observability Foundation - Structured logging, request IDs, context-aware logging\n- 0.4: Configuration Framework - TOML schema, parser, validator, config-first development\n- 0.5: Test Infrastructure - Test frameworks, certificate helpers, mock servers, fixtures\n- 0.6: Context Propagation - Context helpers, timeout patterns, value propagation\n- 0.7: Project Scaffolding - Go module, directory structure, Makefile, CI basics\n- 0.8: Graceful Shutdown - Shutdown manager, signal handling, resource cleanup\n\nThis phase invests 15-20% more time upfront but saves 50-80% in rework by catching design issues early and ensuring consistent patterns.","acceptance_criteria":"- All core interfaces defined and documented with godoc\n- Error framework complete with tests\n- Logging outputs structured JSON with request IDs\n- Configuration loads and validates from TOML\n- Test infrastructure functional (can run tests)\n- CI pipeline runs tests automatically\n- Context helpers work correctly\n- Shutdown manager tested\n- golangci-lint configured and passing\n- go vet passing\n- Project structure matches spec\n- No feature code written yet (only foundation)","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:07:31.615729-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-28T17:26:24.65537-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-28T17:26:24.65537-07:00","source_repo":"."}
{"id":"CHAP-i81","content_hash":"6a2f0d64f481e5df229ca43987bc5181d4787c0defe11e27ad1e426f229994c7","title":"Implement env: secret provider","description":"Implement environment variable secret provider that retrieves secrets from process environment.","design":"In internal/secrets/:\n- Create env.go with EnvProvider struct\n- Implement Fetch() using os.Getenv()\n- Return ErrSecretNotFound if variable not set\n- Return ErrSecretNotFound if value is empty string\n- Add validation for variable name format\n- Register provider in init()\n- Write comprehensive unit tests","acceptance_criteria":"- env:VAR_NAME retrieves from environment\n- Missing variables return ErrSecretNotFound\n- Empty values return ErrSecretNotFound\n- Provider registered automatically\n- Unit tests cover all cases (exists, missing, empty)","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:55:23.138219-07:00","updated_at":"2025-12-01T03:12:12.49993-07:00","closed_at":"2025-12-01T03:12:12.49993-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-i81","depends_on_id":"CHAP-8ft","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:55:23.140052-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-i81","depends_on_id":"CHAP-txf","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:56:45.486402-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-jds","content_hash":"99db5ab7ce9846411c40b0e8a5f87a71cfb86adf09dd30b79098156293a4ae3b","title":"Implement basic HTTP proxy server","description":"Create basic HTTP proxy server that listens on configured port and handles incoming connections. This is the foundation for all proxy functionality.","design":"In internal/proxy/:\n- Create server.go with Server struct\n- Implement http.Server with custom Handler\n- Add graceful shutdown with context cancellation\n- Add structured logging for server events\n- Handle SIGTERM and SIGINT signals\n- Bind to configured address (default: 127.0.0.1:4010)\n- Add health check endpoint","acceptance_criteria":"- Server starts on configured port\n- Server responds to health check\n- Server logs startup and shutdown events\n- Graceful shutdown completes within timeout\n- Unit test for server lifecycle","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:50:32.718411-07:00","updated_at":"2025-12-01T01:44:06.680789-07:00","closed_at":"2025-12-01T01:44:06.680789-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-jds","depends_on_id":"CHAP-ecl","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:50:32.720504-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-jds","depends_on_id":"CHAP-o0m","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:51:19.509823-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-jds","depends_on_id":"CHAP-6l4","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:51:25.175062-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-jds","depends_on_id":"CHAP-8tw","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:14:25.813201-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-k7d","content_hash":"1bcc03405e0fde08f10d86ea709847f8cb496fbcbfd8f98502ccb4f73ef574f3","title":"Phase 6: Configuration \u0026 CLI - TOML Loading and Commands","description":"Implement TOML configuration loading, validation, and CLI commands (init and run) to make Chaperone operational.","design":"- Select and integrate TOML parsing library\n- Design configuration file schema\n- Implement configuration loading and validation\n- Implement default config path resolution\n- Implement 'chaperone init' command with templates\n- Update 'chaperone run' to load config\n- Create example configs (OpenAI, Anthropic)","acceptance_criteria":"- TOML configuration loads successfully\n- Configuration validation catches errors\n- chaperone init creates valid config file\n- chaperone run loads config and starts server\n- OpenAI template is functional\n- Unit tests for config parsing pass\n- Integration test uses config file","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:49:21.897174-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-28T17:26:36.437764-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-28T17:26:36.437764-07:00","source_repo":"."}
{"id":"CHAP-lwn","content_hash":"3d2fcd14354fc1a1e10fe6bf8d14c9c514367430d9c87320ad369c1559bd512a","title":"Create .gitignore and basic project files","description":"Create .gitignore for Go projects, minimal README.md, and basic Makefile for build automation.","design":".gitignore should include:\n- Go binaries (chaperone, *.exe, etc.)\n- Test files (*.test, *.out)\n- IDE files (.vscode, .idea, etc.)\n- OS files (.DS_Store)\n- Certificate files (*.pem, *.key)\n- Config files (config.toml, but not examples/)\n\nREADME.md should include:\n- Project name and description\n- Status: Under development\n- Link to PROJECT_SPEC.md\n\nMakefile should include:\n- build, test, lint, clean targets","acceptance_criteria":"- .gitignore exists and covers all necessary patterns\n- README.md is clear and informative\n- Makefile has working build target\n- git status shows clean working tree after build","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:50:21.372117-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-26T03:14:06.31003-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-26T03:14:06.31003-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-lwn","depends_on_id":"CHAP-ecl","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:50:21.373563-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-lwn","depends_on_id":"CHAP-zgc","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:51:08.199292-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-na8","content_hash":"358efc9e23dd7f2c75a0d2e4a3ff7c2ac848c9525670435a06a9d0aa46895cb5","title":"Phase 2: MITM Core - Selective TLS Termination","description":"Implement selective TLS MITM for configured domains, including CA certificate generation, dynamic leaf certificate creation, and domain-based routing decisions.","design":"- CA certificate generation and secure storage\n- Dynamic leaf certificate generation (signed by CA)\n- Certificate caching mechanism (sync.Map)\n- Domain matching logic (exact match for MVP)\n- TLS handshake handling (client and upstream)\n- HTTP request/response proxying through TLS\n- Certificate trust validation and documentation","acceptance_criteria":"- CA certificate generated on first run\n- CA stored securely in ~/.config/chaperone/\n- Leaf certificates generated per-domain\n- TLS handshake succeeds with client\n- HTTP requests decrypted and proxied\n- Integration test with api.openai.com succeeds\n- User can manually trust CA certificate","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:48:59.245881-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-26T02:48:59.245881-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-na8","depends_on_id":"CHAP-ecl","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:51:42.133612-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-o0m","content_hash":"4dc0443bfdca92d381d277a8b877171028aecffd2d9b1c54482f442851a7a8c4","title":"Implement basic CLI framework with cobra","description":"Set up cobra CLI framework with root command and basic 'run' command structure. This establishes the command-line interface pattern for the project.","design":"- Install cobra: go get github.com/spf13/cobra\n- Create cmd/chaperone/main.go as entry point\n- Create cmd/chaperone/cmd/ directory for commands\n- Implement root command with version flag\n- Implement basic 'run' command (empty handler for now)\n- Add flag parsing for port and bind address\n- Add structured logging setup","acceptance_criteria":"- chaperone --version shows version\n- chaperone --help shows usage\n- chaperone run --help shows run command help\n- Binary builds successfully\n- Can run chaperone run (even if it does nothing yet)","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:50:27.053515-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-26T03:14:11.936517-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-26T03:14:11.936517-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-o0m","depends_on_id":"CHAP-ecl","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:50:27.055142-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-o0m","depends_on_id":"CHAP-zgc","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:51:13.846098-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-ora","content_hash":"802308f8c195a695edfa7cacab023bd939b357544010a7188a4fb79e86c15bb3","title":"Phase 7: Testing \u0026 Hardening - E2E and Production Validation","description":"Create E2E tests with real APIs, comprehensive integration test suite, streaming validation, concurrent request testing, and production hardening. NOTE: Test INFRASTRUCTURE is in Phase 0.5, this phase is for complete system validation.","design":"NOTE: Basic test infrastructure (testify, helpers, fixtures) is established in Phase 0.5. This phase focuses on complete system validation.\n\nTasks:\n- Write E2E test with real OpenAI API call (requires API key)\n- Test streaming behavior with large response (10MB+ JSON response)\n- Test concurrent requests (100 simultaneous requests)\n- Test error scenarios (secret not found, upstream 500, upstream timeout)\n- Test CA trust workflow (manual trust, verify curl works)\n- Run golangci-lint and fix all issues\n- Run go vet and fix all issues\n- Write comprehensive README.md with quickstart\n- Create example configs for OpenAI and Anthropic\n- Performance benchmarking\n- Security review of error handling and logging","acceptance_criteria":"- Unit tests pass with 80%+ coverage\n- Integration tests pass\n- E2E test successfully calls real API\n- Streaming test shows constant memory usage\n- Concurrent test shows no races (go test -race)\n- golangci-lint passes\n- go vet passes\n- README quickstart is functional\n- Example configs work without modification","notes":"Test infrastructure (Phase 0.5) must complete before this phase. This phase validates the complete, integrated system rather than individual components.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:49:27.550965-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-26T03:11:57.549947-07:00","source_repo":"."}
{"id":"CHAP-pmn","content_hash":"de2c0b73136677e35e52f605e02e3108a445f614f24d51170b35582577f106d5","title":"Phase 0.7: Initialize project scaffolding (Go module, structure, CI)","description":"Initialize Go module and create complete project directory structure. This MUST be first because it creates the foundation for all other work.","design":"Run: go mod init github.com/bmf/chaperone\n\nCreate directories:\n- cmd/chaperone/\n- internal/errors/ (for Phase 0.2)\n- internal/log/ (for Phase 0.3)\n- internal/config/ (for Phase 0.4)\n- internal/context/ (for Phase 0.6)\n- internal/shutdown/ (for Phase 0.8)\n- internal/proxy/ (for Phase 1+)\n- internal/mitm/ (for Phase 2+)\n- internal/service/ (for Phase 3+)\n- internal/secrets/ (for Phase 3+)\n- internal/auth/ (for Phase 4+)\n- internal/audit/ (for Phase 6+)\n- internal/client/ (for Phase 2+)\n- internal/acl/ (future)\n- test/helpers/ (test utilities)\n- test/fixtures/ (test data)\n- test/integration/\n- test/e2e/\n- examples/\n- docs/\n\nCreate Makefile with targets:\n- build: compile binary\n- test: run tests\n- test-race: run tests with race detector\n- lint: run golangci-lint\n- fmt: format code\n- clean: remove artifacts\n\nCreate .golangci.yml for linting configuration\n\nCreate basic .github/workflows/ci.yml (or equivalent CI config)","acceptance_criteria":"- go.mod exists with correct module path\n- All directories created\n- Makefile has all targets and they work\n- .golangci.yml configured\n- CI configuration exists\n- go build runs without errors (even with empty main)\n- make lint runs (even if there's nothing to lint yet)\n- make test runs (even if there are no tests yet)","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:07:50.48613-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-28T17:26:55.480549-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-28T17:26:55.480549-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-pmn","depends_on_id":"CHAP-hbj","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:07:50.488481-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-pzr","content_hash":"8c3ab9ad4c9df90e9419c4709bce8c893318da4dd023c8611ea555d7f113830b","title":"Phase 5: Service Engine - Configuration and Policy","description":"Implement service configuration structures, service registry, and policy enforcement for path/method allowlists and request size limits.","design":"- Define Service and Policy configuration structures\n- Implement service registry (map keyed by host_pattern)\n- Implement service lookup by hostname (exact match)\n- Implement path allowlist checking (glob matching)\n- Implement method allowlist checking\n- Implement request body size limit enforcement\n- Integrate with MITM handler, secret providers, and auth strategies","acceptance_criteria":"- Service config structure defined\n- Service registry loads services\n- Service lookup returns correct service by hostname\n- Path allowlist blocks disallowed paths (403)\n- Method allowlist blocks disallowed methods (403)\n- Body size limit enforced\n- Integration test verifies policy enforcement","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:49:16.234211-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-26T02:49:16.234211-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-pzr","depends_on_id":"CHAP-bwz","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:58:01.931444-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-qkq","content_hash":"a1e440614a18cef6daea036157c866f4999917dbcc0ed6e2cc376be50970109f","title":"Define Service and Policy configuration structures","description":"Design and implement Go structs for service configuration and policy definitions.","design":"In internal/service/:\n- Create types.go with Service and Policy structs\n- Service fields: HostPattern, AuthStrategy, CredentialRef, Policy\n- Policy fields: AllowedMethods, AllowedPaths, MaxBodyBytes, ClientGroups\n- Add JSON/TOML struct tags for config parsing\n- Add validation methods (Validate())\n- Document all fields clearly\n- Add default values for optional fields","acceptance_criteria":"- Structs defined with all required fields\n- Struct tags for TOML parsing\n- Validation methods work\n- Default values applied correctly\n- Unit tests for validation logic","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:55:57.12742-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-30T16:29:46.80991-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-30T16:29:46.80991-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-qkq","depends_on_id":"CHAP-pzr","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:55:57.128683-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-rtn","content_hash":"d5e427f45ee523bd9c0d9b1e48758065b7cb8a30424696bdcc8083354ace69ac","title":"Write integration test for MITM with trusted CA","description":"Create integration test that validates selective MITM works for configured domain (api.openai.com) with generated certificate.","design":"In test/integration/:\n- Create mitm_test.go\n- Generate test CA and trust it in test HTTP client\n- Configure test service for api.openai.com\n- Start chaperone with MITM enabled\n- Make HTTPS request through proxy\n- Verify request reaches upstream\n- Verify response is correct\n- Test that non-configured domains still tunnel\n- Test certificate validation failures","acceptance_criteria":"- Test generates and trusts test CA\n- MITM works for configured domain\n- Non-configured domains use transparent tunnel\n- Certificate presented is signed by test CA\n- HTTP request/response work end-to-end\n- Test cleans up resources\n- No certificate errors in test client","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:53:11.127809-07:00","updated_at":"2025-12-01T01:29:22.846201-07:00","closed_at":"2025-12-01T01:29:22.846201-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-rtn","depends_on_id":"CHAP-na8","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:53:11.129769-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-rtn","depends_on_id":"CHAP-90r","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:54:05.606783-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-txf","content_hash":"4facb6aa50cf49287478e67d1479e4447f8910f0642ac6de855da15f33b29bf4","title":"Verify SecretProvider interface and add provider registry","description":"Verify the SecretProvider interface from Phase 0.1 meets implementation needs. Add credential_ref parser and provider registry infrastructure.","design":"NOTE: The SecretProvider interface is ALREADY DEFINED in Phase 0.1 (CHAP-dhf). This task adds the supporting infrastructure.\n\nIn internal/secrets/:\n- Review provider.go interface from Phase 0.1\n- Implement credential_ref parser (splits protocol:path)\n  - Example: env:OPENAI_API_KEY -\u003e protocol=\"env\", path=\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"\n  - Example: file:/path/to/secret.txt -\u003e protocol=\"file\", path=\"/path/to/secret.txt\"\n- Create provider registry (map[string]SecretProvider)\n- Add Register(name string, provider SecretProvider) function\n- Add Get(protocol string) (SecretProvider, error) function\n- Add Fetch(ctx context.Context, ref string) (string, error) convenience function that:\n  1. Parses credential_ref\n  2. Gets provider from registry\n  3. Calls provider.Fetch()\n\nError types (ErrSecretNotFound, ErrPermissionDenied, ErrTimeout) are defined in Phase 0.2.\n\nWrite tests:\n- credential_ref parser tests (various formats)\n- Provider registration tests\n- Provider retrieval tests\n- Full Fetch() flow tests","acceptance_criteria":"- credential_ref parser splits correctly\n- Parser handles edge cases (missing colon, multiple colons, etc.)\n- Provider registry stores and retrieves providers\n- Fetch() convenience function works end-to-end\n- Test coverage \u003e= 85%\n- go test -race passes","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:55:17.453486-07:00","updated_at":"2025-12-01T03:12:06.806399-07:00","closed_at":"2025-12-01T03:12:06.806399-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-txf","depends_on_id":"CHAP-8ft","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:55:17.456424-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-txf","depends_on_id":"CHAP-dhf","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T03:12:33.725578-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-vwg","content_hash":"f441062f31fc97f257764212a8a279841cf3918b3efda4e40179437f5d70d795","title":"Implement secret caching with TTL","description":"Implement secret caching layer with 5-minute TTL to reduce provider calls while allowing rotation.","design":"In internal/secrets/:\n- Create cache.go with CachedProvider wrapper\n- Use sync.Map for concurrent access\n- Store tuple: (secret string, expireAt time.Time)\n- On Fetch(): check cache first, return if not expired\n- If expired or missing: call underlying provider, cache result\n- Set TTL to 5 minutes (configurable)\n- Wrap all providers with caching automatically\n- Add cache invalidation function\n- Add cache stats (hits, misses)","acceptance_criteria":"- Cache returns cached value within TTL\n- Cache calls provider after TTL expires\n- Cache works correctly under concurrent load\n- Cache invalidation works\n- Unit tests verify TTL behavior\n- No race conditions (go test -race passes)","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:55:34.461747-07:00","updated_at":"2025-12-01T03:12:24.16266-07:00","closed_at":"2025-12-01T03:12:24.16266-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-vwg","depends_on_id":"CHAP-8ft","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:55:34.463359-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-w9q","content_hash":"2155b806abe7b3e16e2cb7a4082574a6d9c8dadd0bbafd94ba41e7799b183187","title":"Implement dynamic leaf certificate generation","description":"Generate per-domain TLS certificates on-demand, signed by local CA, with appropriate Subject Alternative Names.","design":"In internal/mitm/:\n- Create cert.go with certificate generation\n- Generate RSA 2048-bit key per domain\n- Create certificate signed by CA\n- Set Subject CN to hostname\n- Add SAN (Subject Alternative Name) for hostname\n- Set 90-day validity period\n- Implement certificate caching (sync.Map)\n- Cache key: hostname string\n- Handle wildcard domains (*.example.com)\n- Add certificate serial number tracking","acceptance_criteria":"- Certificate generated for given hostname\n- Certificate signed by CA (verifiable)\n- SAN includes correct hostname\n- Certificate cached correctly\n- Subsequent requests use cached cert\n- Unit tests for cert generation\n- Wildcard certificates work (if needed)","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:52:37.483806-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-30T17:04:11.307705-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-30T17:04:11.307705-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-w9q","depends_on_id":"CHAP-na8","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:52:37.485364-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-w9q","depends_on_id":"CHAP-5v5","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:53:27.952268-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-zgc","content_hash":"cc56685773c4bad6a2bcba955130d7ae408b645a16a5510fab77c5580ea2a46d","title":"Initialize Go module and project structure","description":"Initialize Go module with path github.com/bmf/chaperone and create complete project directory structure following Go best practices.","design":"Run: go mod init github.com/bmf/chaperone\nCreate directories:\n- cmd/chaperone/\n- internal/proxy/\n- internal/mitm/\n- internal/service/\n- internal/secrets/\n- internal/auth/\n- internal/audit/\n- internal/config/\n- internal/client/\n- internal/acl/\n- examples/\n- docs/\n- test/integration/\n- test/e2e/\n- scripts/","acceptance_criteria":"- go.mod exists with correct module path\n- All directories created\n- Directory structure matches specification\n- go build runs without errors (even with empty main)","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:50:15.706713-07:00","updated_at":"2025-11-26T03:11:18.761559-07:00","closed_at":"2025-11-26T03:11:18.761559-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-zgc","depends_on_id":"CHAP-ecl","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:50:15.708622-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
{"id":"CHAP-znp","content_hash":"a7166c3cb5674329cd4801dcb415b8b3806682b329a07fa7dbf99e42f83b8563","title":"Implement header template auth strategy","description":"Implement header template strategy for injecting custom headers like X-API-Key.","design":"In internal/auth/:\n- Create header.go with HeaderStrategy struct\n- Accept configuration: header_name (e.g., \"X-API-Key\")\n- Implement Apply() method\n- Set configured header with secret as value\n- Support template syntax for future (e.g., \"Bearer {secret}\")\n- Handle existing header (replace it)\n- Register strategy as \"header\"\n- Write unit tests","acceptance_criteria":"- Custom header set correctly\n- Header name configurable\n- Header value is secret\n- Existing header replaced\n- Template expansion works (if implemented)\n- Unit tests verify all scenarios","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:55:51.463428-07:00","updated_at":"2025-12-01T05:02:34.488811-07:00","closed_at":"2025-12-01T05:02:34.488811-07:00","source_repo":".","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"CHAP-znp","depends_on_id":"CHAP-bwz","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:55:51.464787-07:00","created_by":"bmf"},{"issue_id":"CHAP-znp","depends_on_id":"CHAP-2oe","type":"blocks","created_at":"2025-11-26T02:57:02.413069-07:00","created_by":"bmf"}]}
